### [embed()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}

::: {.doc-subject}

Generate embeddings for a sequence of texts.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/raghilda/blob/docs-embedding-providers/src/raghilda/_embedding.py#L156-L179){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
embed(x, input_type=EmbedInputType.DOCUMENT)
```
:::

#### Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[x]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Sequence[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A sequence of texts to generate embeddings for.

<code>[input_type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [EmbedInputType]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [EmbedInputType.DOCUMENT]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The type of input being embedded. Some models (e.g., Cohere) produce
    different embeddings for queries vs documents. Default is DOCUMENT.
:::

#### Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Sequence[Sequence[float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A sequence of embeddings (the same length as `x`), where each embedding is
    a sequence of floats.
:::

